- Amazon (and apparently Amazon.co.uk) is selling the correct
version, entirely without us having to do anything further

- The correct version, in all its formats, is at
https://mw.lojban.org/papri/The_Complete_Lojban_Language ; for those
of you who were wondering why I sunk years of my life into this,
note that every version listed there is fundamentally identical and
generated from the same source, so if you want to update all of
theme there's only one place you have to change.

- The current versions are hosted in two clear places;
http://lojban.org/publications/cll/ and
https://github.com/lojban/cll/tree/docbook-prince/official ; the
point there is that we should never have to wonder ever again where
the files we sent to the printer went (as has happened in the past
at least twice)

- All of the old files (examples:
http://www.lojban.org/publications/reference_grammar/chapter1.html
and http://lojban.org/publications/refgram_chunked/cllc/2/8/ )
hosted on my servers now point to the new/correct place

